From 85361e113b1bdc71fd538380d1769042de84675d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:28:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] Reservations taken together, and larger commits where
 none is charged (#2873)

A compile reserves about 33 arenas, each by an mmap of its own, and
commits each by mprotect calls that start at 64 KB: a small unit made 36
mmap and 51 mprotect calls.

Where the address space is unlimited and the command fixed its limits, a
reservation takes its mapping from a region mapped once for its mmap
flags (8 TiB each, inaccessible, carved from the start): what it gets
is what its own mmap gave it, and its release unmaps it or its pool
keeps it. A finite RLIMIT_AS, compact reservations, a sanitizer's build,
a refused or full region and a pool that makes its arenas inaccessible
again leave each reservation its own mapping.

Where the kernel charges no commit (read once, with the limits), a
commit takes the arena's base pages at once, up to 16 MiB, and then four
times what is committed. Where it charges, 64 KB and doubling, as before.

A hello.c compile here: 7 mmap calls and 35 mprotect calls, and four
calls to read the commit policy; the same object.

Part of #2873.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NNmNQsSoUunkrTyxkuSxop
Signed-off-by: David Gonzalez Martin <davidgmbb@gmail.com>
---
